{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495326-my-first-chronicle-wish-me-luck","id":1495326,"title":"My first chronicle - Wish me luck","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-20T13:36:53-07:00","id":1495326,"title":"My first chronicle - Wish me luck","content":"I don\u2019t really have a question or anything, just want some support for my anxiety. Don\u2019t get me wrong, I\u2019m eager and excited. But at the same time I feel insecure. I\u2019m not a really experienced GM and not quite an experienced as a player either. I don\u2019t have much experience with WoD.<br /> <br /> Since my players are also newbies to MtA, I was planning to run a sort of tutorial: we play a prologue as sleepers, after which the characters have their awakening. Then they would be approached by the local chantry, and invited in for training (they might have to find teachers from further away). The story would revolve around the peculiar fact of four simultaneous awakenings in the same location: why did that happen? The characters would go after some scribblings of an old mage who foresaw a time of mass awakenings, to understand their unique position in the Ascension War. The exact plot is still vague, since I expect the first few sessions be more training and tutorial than a hunt for the McGuffin.<br /> <br /> Any tips? I know the plot might be a bit over the top, but I\u2019m not coming up with something more street level. Obviously, an awakening of four mages at once is a huge deal for the local community (especially since the setting is quite a small city - I want a local game taking place in my home city, that I know well) so it\u2019s natural that this is a major element in the plot.<br /> <br /> I really like the tutorial idea, where the characters would (probably) join Traditions in-game. However, I\u2019m struggling in giving each character a fair chance in finding a teacher. The character concepts would direct to a cross-tradition cabal, and as mentioned, the local community is small. Would a Hermetic chantry leader help an awakend martial arts hobbyist or a hacker find a teacher in Akashic brotherhood or VA? (The latter should be easier, since the training would naturally happen online)?<br /> <br /> What pitfalls do you see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27571,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27571-maestrim","user":"Maestrim","date":".  Typos 10-20-2022, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27571-maestrim","name":"Maestrim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T16:44:23-07:00","id":1495335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maestrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495326-my-first-chronicle-wish-me-luck#post1495326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t really have a question or anything, just want some support for my anxiety. Don\u2019t get me wrong, I\u2019m eager and excited. But at the same time I feel insecure. I\u2019m not a really experienced GM and not quite an experienced as a player either. I don\u2019t have much experience with WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simulating the universe as a limited human is a challenge for which a little bit of anxiety is to be expected. Maybe do some physical exercise before the session, if not the same day, the day before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maestrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495326-my-first-chronicle-wish-me-luck#post1495326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since my players are also newbies to MtA, I was planning to run a sort of tutorial: we play a prologue as sleepers, after which the characters have their awakening. Then they would be approached by the local chantry, and invited in for training (they might have to find teachers from further away). The story would revolve around the peculiar fact of four simultaneous awakenings in the same location: why did that happen? The characters would go after some scribblings of an old mage who foresaw a time of mass awakenings, to understand their unique position in the Ascension War. The exact plot is still vague, since I expect the first few sessions be more training and tutorial than a hunt for the McGuffin.<br /> <br /> Any tips? I know the plot might be a bit over the top, but I\u2019m not coming up with something more street level. Obviously, an awakening of four mages at once is a huge deal for the local community (especially since the setting is quite a small city - I want a local game taking place in my home city, that I know well) so it\u2019s natural that this is a major element in the plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you give the players a prophetic text predicting mass awakenings, they will expect mass awakenings during the story. Do you want the chronicle to become one where everyone is talking about magic being real? What if the text mainly predicts <i>their</i> awakenings? To make the job of storytelling easier, ask each player how their character would change the world if they could. Let them determine what type of cabal they are going to be. That tells you what kind of plot content you want to create for the sessions to follow. If someone says they are for reducing economic inequality, create a Syndicate Mage who traps sleepers with high interest payday loans, for example.<br /> <br /> Playing in a familiar town is a good start. You should intensify problems that exist. If there is poverty or homelessness, then there is pressure to build new housing, which usually involves deforestation. You can put members of the Chantry on conflicting sides of the issue. Same with the nearest Technocracy Construct.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maestrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495326-my-first-chronicle-wish-me-luck#post1495326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the tutorial idea, where the characters would (probably) join Traditions in-game. However, I\u2019m struggling in giving each character a fair chance in finding a teacher. The character concepts would direct to a cross-tradition cabal, and as mentioned, the local community is small. Would a Hermetic chantry leader help an awakend martial arts hobbyist or a hacker find a teacher in Akashic brotherhood or VA? (The latter should be easier, since the training would naturally happen online)?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your game is Friday Night and you want the players to meet their mentors fairly soon, there are two options.<br /> 1) Invent a mentor for each in the next day. For this, I would do searches for old posts by storytellers asking about mentors. I know I replied to one in the last year or so. You could also post a reply in this thread asking for mentor ideas. Specify the Traditions involved.<br /> <br /> 2) Have an effect that obscures the real appearance and voice of people meeting in the Chantry for security reasons. I did a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1422832-chantry-common-areas-anonymizing-appearances\">post</a> about this. The Mentors can still impart knowledge without revealing much about themselves.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maestrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495326-my-first-chronicle-wish-me-luck#post1495326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What pitfalls do you see?</div> </div> </div> </div>Specific to your campaign, there is no antagonist to drive conflict. Besides training, there could be conversation in the Chantry that points to the question of an antagonist. A player might ask, &quot;Are there any threats or problems in the area?&quot;. I would come up with just one sympathetic sleeper who has suffered terribly as a result of a mage antagonist's magic. They could be asked to go and interview the sleeper.<br /> <br /> Generally, in a modern MtA setting, the biggest pitfall is Guns and Health Levels. A single gunshot can easily kill a character and you never know when combat might happen. For this, have the Technocracy use non-lethal weapons to attempt to capture their out-faction rivals, since captured enemies are worth more than dead ones.<br /> <br /> Another is &quot;Node Wars&quot;. If there are too many Nodes dotting the land, the strategy of attacking other faction's Nodes to take them over can occur to players, which reduces the depth of the game when done repeatedly. I Make Nodes rare and allow for other ways to get Quintessence. Making them rare also lets you put more detail into each one, avoiding Nodes becoming generic.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 3, teleportation. That's an issue I communicated with a player about from the beginning. If they frequently decide to teleport to foreign countries and ask for description while the other players are waiting around, it derails the game. There should be a good reason for long range teleportation. I give it an automatic point of Paradox, which also discourages overuse.<br /> <br /> As long as you are working with your players to build a story, it will go well. If you make a mistake, be honest and retcon it out or &quot;erase-rewind&quot;.<br /> <br /> Good Luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-20-2022, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[